<title>USA: Berkshire Mortgage Finance to buy mortgage firm.</title>
<headline>Berkshire Mortgage Finance to buy mortgage firm.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berkshire Mortgage Finance said Wednesday it had reached an agreement with The Patrician Financial Co for it to acquire Patrician before the end of the year.</p>
<p>Berkshire, a multi-family lender, said the acquisition would create a portfolio worth nearly $4.0 billion, half of which will be Fannie Mae DUS loans.</p>
<p>It said Patrician, a commercial mortgage firm, would continue to operate out of its Bethesda, Maryland offices, led by its founder, Gaye Beasley.</p>
<p>Berkshire belongs to The Berkshire Group of Boston.</p>
</text>
